<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">St Donatian's Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sint-Donaaskathedraal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St Donatian's Cathedral was the principal church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a>, standing on the Burg square beside the counts' residence. A collegiate church dedicated to Saint Donatian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a>, it was where Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-good">Charles the Good</a> was murdered in 1127, and it became the cathedral of the new diocese of Bruges in 1559. It was sold and demolished after the French annexation, from 1799.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-donatians-cathedral.jpg" alt="St Donatian's Cathedral" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcus Gerards · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brugge_-_Waterhalle_1294_-_1787.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
